Most players learn this lesson the hard way at some point.

In many situations it is perfectly possible to win after blowing up a
bag of holding, although, if you don't have another bag around, you'll
have to be pretty careful to travel light. Remember that not lugging
everything around with you not only keeps you fast but also gives you
that little bit of insurance against screwing up and destroying parts of
your inventory.

>Will Mjollner work throughout the whole game? It seems like a solid
>weapon, but I'm wondering if I shouldn't be looking for something
>better later(I haven't made it to the "later" stages, but I'm just
>wondering for the future).

As others have already pointed out, it's not the most popular of
artifact weapons. That said, it's not out of the question to ascend with
it in a pinch, so you can certainly leave it until later to worry about
it. Unless you're lawful you can't get Excalibur in any particularly
sensible way, and the other good artifact weapons are either randomly
generated or only likely to turn up much later on.

